== Android platform work ==

Android Open Source Project — Google LLC and contributors. Apache License 2.0.
    https://source.android.com/
    Remora builds Android images from AOSP sources. The images are AOSP's work; Remora's patch
    series (vendor/source-patches/) modifies it and is distributed under this project's licence.

LineageOS — the LineageOS project and contributors. Apache License 2.0.
    https://lineageos.org/
    The image family Remora builds by default derives from LineageOS.

Linux kernel — no entry needed. A Remora image carries no kernel: the container runs on the
    host's, and a built image contains no kernel image and no kernel modules. There is therefore
    no GPL v2 kernel source to offer with one (docs/adr/0001-own-the-stack.md).

redroid — its authors. Apache License 2.0.  https://github.com/remote-android/redroid-doc
    Remora's device tree and container-compatibility patches began as this project's work.

scrcpy — Genymobile and Romain Vimont. Apache License 2.0.
    https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy
    Remora no longer ships any scrcpy code. Its mirror protocol reuses scrcpy 4.0's control
    message, device message and stream framing BYTE LAYOUTS, which are specified in
    docs/MIRROR_PROTOCOL.md; that reuse is the reason this entry remains.


== Redistribution of built images ==

An Android image built with Remora is not automatically redistributable. Whether it can be shared
depends entirely on which features were enabled:

  - Google Apps and Widevine are proprietary, and no licence grants their redistribution.
  - The ARM native-bridge libraries are proprietary, likewise.
  - Magisk is GPL v3; redistributing an image containing it carries a source-availability
    obligation, met by offering the matching release (github.com/topjohnwu/Magisk, tag v30.7).
  - The Play-integrity / root-hiding components are mixed: ReZygisk and PlayIntegrityFork are
    GPL v3, Shamiko is closed-source with no licence at all. Audit each component before sharing
    an image that includes them.

docs/IMAGE_MIRROR.md records, tag by tag, which of these a Remora-built image carries and the
source offers that must accompany it.
